usage: platform_stack_smoke.py [-h] [--no-build] [--keep] [--tag TAG]
                               [--jobs JOBS] [--log-dir LOG_DIR]
                               [--attach PROJECT] [--env-file ENV_FILE]
                               [--sim-version SIM_VERSION] [--website ORIGIN]
                               [--match-e2e]

Smoke test of the self-hosted platform stack (deploy/compose.yaml).

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --no-build            use already built images with --tag
  --keep                leave the project running
  --tag TAG             image tag to build and run (default: smoke)
  --jobs JOBS           C++ build jobs
  --log-dir LOG_DIR     write compose logs and results.json here
  --attach PROJECT      check this running Compose project instead
  --env-file ENV_FILE   with --attach: the deployment's env file
  --sim-version SIM_VERSION
                        with --attach: expected sim version key (default: this
                        checkout)
  --website ORIGIN      with --attach: separately hosted public website whose
                        old app paths redirect here
  --match-e2e           also play a rated quick match through relay,
                        verification and ratings
